<title>UK: GA down as Capel advises &quot;take profits&quot;.</title>
<headline>GA down as Capel advises &quot;take profits&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in General Accident Plc dropped on Tuesday as analysts at HSBC James Capel advised taking profits on the stock and switching into Royal Sun Alliance Plc, dealers said.</p>
<p>Shares in GA, up 9.4 percent in the previous three sessions, were down 16p at 856 by 1301 GMT in volume of 2.7 million shares, while Royal Sun was up 5p at 505 in volume of just under three million shares.</p>
<p>Capel analysts were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
